.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt FORK 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fork ,
.Nm vfork
.Nd create a new process
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In unistd.h
.Ft pid_t
.Fn fork void
.Ft pid_t
.Fn vfork void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn fork creates a child process. .Fn vfork is the historical shared-address variant; in
RavenBSD it follows the same process-creation path as .Fn fork.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The parent receives the child pid; the child receives 0. On failure -1 is returned.
.Sh ERRORS
Until process cloning is provided, both functions return -1 with .Er ENOSYS.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr posix_spawn 3 ,
.Xr libc 7
.Sh STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2024; ring 0.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Fn fork returns -1 with .Er ENOSYS until the platform provides process cloning. .Fn vfork
follows the same rule unless C53 documents a narrower fallback.
See H-18 and C53.
